        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: नाराज़",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "नाराज़ — nārāz — \"cross; displeased\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पिता अरुण से नाराज़ थे क्योंकि वह देर से आया। pitā Aruṇ se nārāz the kyoṁki vah der se āyā. Arun's father was cross with him because he came late."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "नाराज़ (nārāz) is usually traced to Persian nārāz, \"displeased\", built on nā-, \"not\", and a word for \"content\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
